From 00b68eb6159291a80eeefc537f82052bc38ef662 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mike Kinney <mike.kinney@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 13:03:45 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] docs(guide): describe the user-visible changes merged since
 v0.27.0

The user guide now describes each user-visible change that merged
after v0.27.0: the tool library window, the Recipes tab, the holder
library and the Holders page, tool components and stacks, new machine
file keys, the laser kind, post controller details (Fanuc, Doosan DNM,
Haas, Siemens, Mach3, Mach4, LinuxCNC, Tormach, Heidenhain, Sodick),
start and exit picks, 2D and 3D operation changes, Rotary Flow sets,
stock simulation changes, DXF blocks, SolidCraft face names, and the
accessibility and refusal wording changes.

The manifest table of the post-processor reference gets the
manualToolChange row (#4114). This makes the existing site test
test_manifest_properties_have_reference_rows green.

The pin site/tests/test_release_028_guide.py asserts the key facts of
each change in its section.

Fixes #4439

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
